course: dictionary
lesson: 10970
title: Wane: the Moon and beyond
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Wane is a word with two main meanings. The first is about the Moon. «A waning moon grows smaller.» After the full moon, the Moon looks smaller each night, so wane means to shrink little by little.
explain: The second meaning is about strength, size or importance. «His interest began to wane.» This means his interest got weaker bit by bit, not all at once. Interest, light and strength can all wane.
explain: The opposite of wane is wax. The Moon waxes (grows) from new moon to full moon, then wanes (shrinks) back. Wax and wane go together as a pair, so if you know one, you can often work out the other.
fact: Wane means to become smaller or weaker little by little.
fact: «Waning» means shrinking, and «waxing» means growing.
fact: «On the wane» means getting weaker or becoming less common.
fact: The Moon goes from new moon to full moon and back to new moon in about 29 and a half days.
fact: A waning crescent is the thin Moon that you can see just before the new moon.
exercise: «A waning moon grows smaller each night.» What does waning mean here? | Shining the brightest | Turning red | *Getting smaller | Growing bigger
exercise: «His interest began to wane.» What does this tell us? | He was very cold | His interest suddenly grew very strong | He lost his bag | *His interest got weaker, bit by bit
exercise: Which word means the opposite of wane, as in the Moon growing each night? | shrink | fade | dim | *wax
test: The Moon waxes from new moon to full moon. What does it do next, on the way back to new? | *wanes | rises | sets | waxes
test: Which phrase means getting weaker? | under the stars | *on the wane | in the sky | at full moon
exam: Lucy watches the Moon each night. «It looks smaller now than last week.» Which word fits best for what the Moon is doing? | Waxing | Full | *Waning | New
